				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>On this day, January 30, 1990, 25 years ago, <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s <strong>Keep It Together </strong>was released!<br />
This is the 6th single from masterpiece album <strong>Like A Prayer</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Keep It Together</strong> is a pop and funk song with an upbeat rhythm and groove. It was produced by Madonna and Bray, and features Paulinho da Costa on percussion, brass playing by David Boruff and Steven Madaio, Bill Bottrell as the audio engineer and guitars by Chester Kamen. Despite not on the album&#8217;s credits, <strong>Prince</strong> also played guitar on the song according to <strong>Madonna</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Keep It Together</strong> peaked at #<strong>8</strong> on the <strong>Billboard Hot 100</strong> and topped the Hot Dance Music/Club Play chart.<br />
Three months since its release, it was certified <strong>gold</strong> by the RIAA for <strong>500,000</strong> copies.<br />
In Australia, Keep It Together went #1 (for five weeks) on the ARIA Singles Chart. It was certified <strong>double-platinum</strong> by the ARIA for <strong>140,000</strong> copies.</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/happy-25th-anniversary-keep-together/20150130">Happy 25th anniversary Keep It Together!</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
