				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>On this day, November 21, 2000, 14 years ago <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s <strong>Don&#8217;t Tell Me</strong> was released.</p>
<blockquote><p>&#8216;Don&#8217;t Tell Me&#8217; was the most unlikely follow-up to 2000&#8217;s &#8216;Music&#8217;. Stop-and-go guitar riffs, an atypical structure and peculiar lyrics (&#8216;Tell the bed not to lay/Like the open mouth of a grave/Not to stare up at me/Like a calf down on its knees&#8217;) made it an unlikely hit to boot. But a hit is exactly what it was, earning Madonna her 27th Top 5 hit and 24th gold single (tying the Beatles). &#8220;Don&#8217;t Tell Me&#8221; found Madonna at her most soulful, with a vocal performance reminiscent of the forceful tone of &#8216;Express Yourself&#8217;.</p></blockquote>
<p> Sal Cinquemani from Slant Magazine commented Don&#8217;t Tell Me.</p>
<p><strong>Don&#8217;t Tell Me</strong> peaked at <strong>#4</strong> on the Billboard Hot 100 and was certified Gold.<br />
Also in the UK the song peaked at <strong>#4</strong> and has sold more than <strong>185.000</strong> copies so far.<br />
<strong>Don&#8217;t Tell Me</strong> has sold <strong>4.500.000</strong> units worldwide so far.</p>
