		<description><![CDATA[<p>On this day, November 17, 1987, 27 years ago, Madonna&#8216;s first remix album You Can Dance was released. Remixing is [...]</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/day-madonnas-can-dance-released-27-years-ago/20141117">On this day: Madonna&#8217;s You Can Dance was released 27 years ago.</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>On this day, November 17, 1987, 27 years ago, <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s first remix album <strong>You Can Dance </strong>was released.</p>
<blockquote><p>Remixing is a form of secondary creativity. Dance music elevates the DJ and the mixer to being almost on a level with the musician. In my opinion this is false. Manipulation of pre-recorded sound sources may be creative in a secondary sense, and may be valid in its own field, but it is pseudo musicianship. That&#8217;s why we tried to have a fresh approach to the songs for You Can Dance, as if we were developing and composing them for the first time.</p></blockquote>
<p>—<strong>Patrick Leonard</strong> talking about working on the album.</p>
<p><strong>Spotlight</strong> was the only single released from the album in Japan, but charted on the Billboard airplay chart thanks to radio play (it peaked at #32).</p>
<p><strong>You Can Dance</strong> peaked at <strong>#14</strong> on the Billboard 200 and was certified Platinum for <strong>1.000.000</strong> copies sold.<br />
In UK the album peaked at <strong>#5</strong> and was certified Platinum by the for <strong>300.000 </strong>units.<br />
<strong>You Can Dance</strong> has sold more than <strong>5.000.000</strong> worldwide and became the <strong>2nd best-selling remix album of all time</strong> (behind Michael Jackson&#8217; Blood on the Dance Floor: HIStory in the Mix).</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/day-madonnas-can-dance-released-27-years-ago/20141117">On this day: Madonna&#8217;s You Can Dance was released 27 years ago.</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
