				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>On this day, November 12, 1984, <strong>30</strong> years ago, <strong>Like A Virgin</strong>, <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s 2nd studio album, was released!</p>
<blockquote><p><strong>Like a Virgin</strong> is a much harder album, much more aggressive than the first record. The songs on that were pretty weak. On this one I&#8217;ve chosen all the songs and I want them to be all hits—no fillers. That&#8217;s why I&#8217;ve done outside songs as well as six of my own&#8230; I wanted every song to be strong.</p></blockquote>
<p>—<strong>Madonna</strong>, about the songs in Like a Virgin.</p>
<p>The album entered the Billboard 200 at #3 and it peaked at <strong>#1</strong> on February 9, 1985, where it stayed for three weeks. <strong>Like A Virgin</strong> was certified <strong>Diamond</strong> for selling more than <strong>10.000.000</strong> units.<br />
In the UK, <strong>Like a Virgin</strong> debuted at #74 (can you believe it?) and it peaked at <strong>#1</strong> on September 1985. The album has sold more than <strong>900.000</strong> copies and was certified <strong>3xPlatinum</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Like A Virgin</strong> worldwide has sold more than <strong>21.000.000</strong> copies.</p>
<p>The singles released are:<br />
&#8220;Like a Virgin&#8221;, &#8220;Material Girl&#8221;, &#8220;Angel&#8221;, &#8220;Into the Groove&#8221;, &#8220;Dress You Up&#8221;.</p>
<p>Which is your favourite track?</p>
