				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>On this day, November 9, 1990, 24 years ago, <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s first greatest hits, <strong>The Immaculate Collection</strong>, was released.<br />
The album was ranked at number one on the Blender magazine&#8217;s list of &#8220;100 Greatest American Albums of All Time&#8221;.</p>
<p>In UK The Immaculate Collection stayed at #<strong>1</strong> for nine weeks, becoming the biggest selling UK album in 1990, breaking the record for the longest consecutive weeks at #1 by a solo female artist, at that time.<br />
The album has sold <strong>3,665,068</strong> so far in UK and is certified 12xPlatinum!</p>
<p>In USA the album peaked at #<strong>2</strong> and it stayed in the chart for 142 weeks.<br />
It was certified Diamond for more than <strong>10,000,000</strong> copies sold (her second Diamond album).</p>
<p>Worldwide the album has sold more than <strong>30,000,000</strong> copies becoming Madonna&#8217;s best selling album, and it is also the best-selling compilation album ever released by a solo artist.</p>
