				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>On this day, November 6, 1990, 24 years ago, <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s <strong>Justify My Love</strong> was released.<br />
<a href="http://www.ew.com/ew/article/0,,315180,00.html" target="_blank">The song was written by <strong>Lenny Kravitz</strong> and <strong>Ingrid Chavez</strong>, with additional lyrics by <strong>Madonna</strong></a>.<br />
<strong>Justify My Love</strong> is one of Madonna&#8217;s most controversial songs to date. As a result of all the controversy, the single was released as a video-single and became one of the the highest selling video single of all time. </p>
<p>The song peaked at <strong>#1</strong> on the <strong>Billboard Hot 100</strong> and it was certified <strong>Platinum</strong>.<br />
In UK it peaked at #2, selling 235.000 so far.<br />
<strong>Justify My Love</strong> has sold more than <strong>2.000.000</strong> units worldwide so far.</p>
<p>The video was deemed too sexually explicit for MTV and was banned from the network.<br />
That&#8217;s what Madonna said about the banning: </p>
<blockquote><p>Why is it that people are willing to go and watch a movie about someone getting blown to bits for no reason at all, and nobody wants to see two girls kissing and two men snuggling?</p></blockquote>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/day-madonnas-justify-love-released-24-years-ago/20141106">On this day: Madonna&#8217;s &#8220;Justify My Love&#8221; was released 24 years ago!</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
